    "created_at": "2016-02-05T06:50:34Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-02-05T06:51:27Z",
    "body": "That looks pretty great! I hadn't noticed how terrible https://mediasession.spec.whatwg.org/#examples looks, it's a pretty stark comparison. Nice that you also included the CSS, it's like the IDL blocks now.\n\nHow did you do the syntax highlighting, added manually for testing? I think that we can make changes one step at a time, and syntax highlighting will presumably require either using a build-time parser of the various languages integrated with at least wattsi and bikeshed, or doing it in JavaScript in a way that doesn't slow down the initial load.\n\nAbout the visuals, I think it's mostly about tweaking the padding so that the result is not too spacious and the colors. Although notes currently have very little padding because they're often one-liners, there are a some big notes (the \"domintro\" blocks) that are all green, and it would be nice if the IDL blocks were more prominent than those.\n\n@annevk, can we set things up so that @rynarud can experiment on the real spec or specs? Maybe something like https://html.spec.whatwg.org/?pretty and https://mediasession.spec.whatwg.org/?pretty that loads an alternative stylesheet?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
